Full_Prompt:
Answer the following question with A, B, C, or D only.

Select the best translation into predicate logic. Some animals are neglected by cruel people. (Ax: x is an animal; Cx: x is cruel; Px: x is a person; Nxy: x neglects y) (A) (∃x)[(Ax • Cx) • (∃y)(Py • Nyx)] (B) (∃x)[(Cx • Px) • (∃y)(Ay • Nxy)] (C) (∃x)[(Ax • Px) • (∃y)(Cy • Nxy)] (D) (∃x)(∃y){[(Ax • Cy) • Py] • Nxy)]}

